This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's explicit request (repeated 4 times identically) was: "продолжай работу по STATE.md" ("continue work per STATE.md"). This is a directive to resume TDD-driven implementation of a Java 8/Maven mini-assistant project ("Коля"-style AI mail agent) exactly where the last session left off, per the project's `STATE.md` snapshot file, following all rules in the root `CLAUDE.md` (Russian-language governance document). No other explicit user requests have been made in this session beyond this repeated continuation instruction. Key constraints from CLAUDE.md that govern all work:
   - Strict TDD: every functional unit needs a failing test commit (RED) followed by a passing implementation commit (GREEN) — minimum two commits per unit, visible in git history.
   - `mvn test` must be green **without** Outlook or JACOB on PATH (JACOB excluded from test classpath via surefire `classpathDependencyExcludes`).
   - Graceful fallbacks everywhere specified: no raw stacktraces to the user, only WARN logs and predictable behavior, for both LLM outages and COM/mail-channel errors.
   - No secrets in code/config/git — env vars only.
   - Structured logs without PII — email bodies must never be logged raw (use `LogEvents.safePreview`).
   - Security review + verification-before-completion required before declaring anything "done" — must actually run `mvn test`/`mvn package` and show output.
   - Atomic, meaningful commits — not one giant commit.
   - Commit locally freely; push after each significant part (per PLAN.md "commit point" markers); never `--no-verify`, `--force` push, or `git reset --hard` without explicit permission.
   - Real LLM/Outlook/JACOB: never installed/used in this dev environment — only `MockLlmClient`/`MockMailChannel` for all development and tests.
   - Journals in `other/agent-logs/`: `STATE.md` (overwritable current snapshot), `PROGRESS.md` (checklist), `DECISIONS.md` (append-only decision log) — must be kept current, especially `STATE.md` at any interruption point.
   - Repository structure: `вводные/` read-only, `project/` is the actual product (git repo pushed to `https://github.com/Serafim96/ai_assesment`), `other/` is working-only material.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Java 8 (Temurin), Maven (local install at `other/tools/apache-maven-3.9.9`), JUnit 4.
   - TDD red→green cycle with git commits per phase task.
   - Tool-calling agent loop pattern (`AgentToolLoop`) with LLM abstraction (`LlmClient`/`MockLlmClient`/`HttpLlmClient`).
   - Idempotency via `SeenStore` (JSON-file backed, atomic writes via `AtomicJsonFileStore`), with "mark before processing, unmark on failure" strategy to survive both duplicate mail-channel deliveries (Outlook sync glitches) and process restarts.
   - `MailProcessingService` orchestration: fetchUnread → seenStore.markIfNew → AgentToolLoop.run → mailChannel.reply, with per-message try/catch so one failure doesn't halt the batch.
   - Graceful degradation: LLM failure and mail-channel failure must never throw out of `processCycle()`, must WARN-log with specific event keys, and must not send automated replies during full LLM outage (to avoid spamming with error text and to allow retry).
   - `AuditLog`: append-only JSONL hash-chain (SHA-256 of seq|eventKey|detailsJson|prevHash), `verify()`/`verifyAndGetFirstCorruptSeq()` — immutability check without HMAC (documented decision in DECISIONS.md as a "hash-chain vs HMAC" deviation).
   - `LogEvents`: PII-safe logging constants (`AGENT_MAIL_SEEN`, `AGENT_TOOL_CALL`, `AGENT_REPLY_SENT`, `LLM_FAILED`, `MAIL_CHANNEL_ERROR`, `AGENT_MAXSTEPS_EXCEEDED`) plus `safePreview(String)` (length + SHA-256 prefix, never raw text) and newly added `jsonEscape(String)` (escapes `"` and `\` for building JSON detail strings, returns `""` for null).
   - Golden scenarios (task.txt §10 / PLAN.md §5): 4 canonical email interactions (add_reminder, find_items, current_datetime, empty/garbage message) — covered in `GoldenScenariosTest`.
   - `Clock.fixed(...)` dependency injection for deterministic date/time testing (avoids flaky "tomorrow" calculations).
   - Session budget tracking (~300k tokens/session) with defined SESSION BREAK points in PLAN.md.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`other/agent-logs/STATE.md`** (read) — showed CP6 done, Phase 7 (T7.1 MailProcessingService, T7.2 golden scenarios) as next step. This was the starting point of the session.

   - **`other/agent-logs/PROGRESS.md`** (read, then edited) — checklist of phases. Edited to mark Phase 7 line as done:
     ```
     - [x] Phase 7 — T7.1 MailProcessingService (идемпотентность+рестарт), T7.2 Golden-сценарии → CP7 → PUSH
     ```
     Phase 8 line (`- [ ] Phase 8 — T8.1 LLM fallback, T8.2 COM fallback, [x] T8.3 PII-маскирование/LogEvents, [x] T8.4 AuditLog(hash-chain) → CP8 → PUSH`) still needs updating once Phase 8 completes — **not yet done**.

   - **`project/PLAN.md`** (read extensively, not modified) — source of truth for Phase 7 and Phase 8 task definitions, golden scenario mapping (§5), session-break table (§6), final checklist (§8), and open decision points (§9). Critical excerpts already quoted above in Key Technical Concepts.

   - **`other/agent-logs/DECISIONS.md`** (read, not yet modified this session) — append-only log; may need a new entry if any deviation arises during Phase 8 (e.g., re: log event key semantics for reply failures), but nothing added yet.

